This project ports the Freebuff tracker from a fork of QuotaBar/OpenUsage by Robin Ebers
(MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Robin Ebers). It is not affiliated with or endorsed by
OpenUsage, and does not use the OpenUsage name or logo as its own.

The legacy model-slug digest (FNV-1a over UTF-16 code units) matches the published
algorithm in Freebuff/Codebuff (Apache License 2.0, Copyright CodebuffAI) so historical
receipts resolve to the same catalog identities. No Freebuff source code is included.

The macOS menu bar app (macos/) follows the SwiftUI panel design of the same QuotaBar fork, and
macos/Sources/FreeTokens/Views/RingSectorShape.swift is ported from it (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026
Robin Ebers).

internal/pricing/pricing_supplement.json is a snapshot of the OpenUsage pricing
supplement (MIT), refreshed at runtime from
https://robinebers.github.io/openusage/pricing_supplement.json.

Third-party Go modules keep their own licenses, listed in go.mod, including:
  fyne.io/systray (Apache-2.0), github.com/creativeprojects/go-selfupdate (MIT),
  modernc.org/sqlite (BSD-3-Clause), github.com/godbus/dbus/v5 (BSD-2-Clause),
  github.com/danieljoos/wincred (MIT), github.com/zalando/go-keyring (MIT),
  github.com/thlib/go-timezone-local (Unlicense or Apache-2.0),
  golang.org/x/sys (BSD-3-Clause).
